01:03:13.236 --> 01:03:15.281
and it's kind of the person who like

01:03:15.281 --> 01:03:17.656
'cause when you're doing it
for yourself and you're acting

01:03:17.656 --> 01:03:20.520
you're in your own head
you're your worst enemy

01:03:20.520 --> 01:03:22.780
'cause you're like, fuck I
should've done it this way.

01:03:22.780 --> 01:03:25.618
'Cause when I recorded for one
of my own videos, 20 takes.

01:03:25.618 --> 01:03:27.810
I record for someone else with a director,

01:03:27.810 --> 01:03:30.430
one or two takes because
they tell me what they want

01:03:30.430 --> 01:03:31.910
and they help me get there

01:03:31.910 --> 01:03:34.453
and a lot of people like
there's 10% of voice actors

01:03:34.453 --> 01:03:37.990
who can deliver lines
amazingly without a director.

01:03:37.990 --> 01:03:40.130
But then there's like
50% who need a director

01:03:40.130 --> 01:03:43.470
and there's like 30, 40% let's be honest,

01:03:43.470 --> 01:03:45.053
they're never gonna get any where with it.

01:03:45.053 --> 01:03:48.400
But it's hard to say that but
it's one of those things where

01:03:48.400 --> 01:03:50.940
you do need like a good
ear somewhat skill.

01:03:50.940 --> 01:03:52.710
- It's a skill, absolutely.
- It's definitely a skill

01:03:52.710 --> 01:03:54.650
'cause I, I personally
think I'm a much better

01:03:54.650 --> 01:03:56.460
voice director than I am a voice actor.

01:03:56.460 --> 01:03:58.320
Even though I've done both.

01:03:58.320 --> 01:03:59.957
I tried to like insert
my own voice as little

01:03:59.957 --> 01:04:02.190
as possible whenever I'm doing kind

01:04:02.190 --> 01:04:04.800
of any kind of voice work
that I've done before

01:04:04.800 --> 01:04:06.894
but I really enjoyed
directing because it's,

01:04:06.894 --> 01:04:09.250
it's definitely a unique skill

01:04:09.250 --> 01:04:11.264
'cause I've seen how
other people direct their

01:04:11.264 --> 01:04:14.037
their work as well and it's
everyone has a different style.

01:04:14.037 --> 01:04:16.362
Some are just not effective at all.

01:04:16.362 --> 01:04:19.530
Some, some, voice
directors, you know, they

01:04:19.530 --> 01:04:20.968
they have no idea what
they want, you know.

01:04:20.968 --> 01:04:24.765
And it's just on the voice actor to save,

01:04:24.765 --> 01:04:26.510
to save the performance somehow,

01:04:26.510 --> 01:04:28.719
even though the director
has no idea what they wants.

01:04:28.719 --> 01:04:30.860
Do you ever get that moment though,

01:04:30.860 --> 01:04:33.333
when you're directing someone and you,

01:04:34.285 --> 01:04:36.910
they've not delivered the line
exactly the way you want it

01:04:36.910 --> 01:04:38.940
and so you have to explain it to them

01:04:38.940 --> 01:04:40.624
and you get to the third point, the third

01:04:40.624 --> 01:04:44.300
it's the third time, the
third time you've tried

01:04:44.300 --> 01:04:47.367
and they still haven't done
it the way you wanted to.

01:04:47.367 --> 01:04:49.410
Do you, do you continue?

01:04:49.410 --> 01:04:51.580
Like do, do, do you continue
trying to explain it to them

01:04:51.580 --> 01:04:53.340
or do you just go with one of the takes?

01:04:53.340 --> 01:04:55.134
- Normally I will do,

01:04:55.134 --> 01:04:57.590
I would try my best to explain it to them.

01:04:57.590 --> 01:04:58.570
- [Garnt] Yeah.

01:04:58.570 --> 01:05:01.440
- Worst case scenario, I'll do a line read

01:05:01.440 --> 01:05:04.160
which a line read is you
don't normally do it.

01:05:04.160 --> 01:05:05.590
It's kind of, it's not unprofessional

01:05:05.590 --> 01:05:08.000
but it wastes a lot of time
which is where the director

01:05:08.000 --> 01:05:09.480
will deliver the line and I'll be like,

01:05:09.480 --> 01:05:10.680
just copy what I just did.

01:05:10.680 --> 01:05:11.513
- [Garnt] Yeah.

01:05:11.513 --> 01:05:13.150
- And that's what I'll do
on the worst case scenario

01:05:13.150 --> 01:05:15.633
and if they can't do that,
then it's like, fuck.

01:05:16.806 --> 01:05:18.420
This is going to be bad.

01:05:18.420 --> 01:05:21.320
Like if they, if they can't
hear one, like what I just did

01:05:21.320 --> 01:05:23.191
and then they can't replicate it

01:05:23.191 --> 01:05:25.215
that means that they have
no idea what I just did.

01:05:25.215 --> 01:05:26.201
- [Garnt] Yeah.
- [Joey] Yeah.

01:05:26.201 --> 01:05:29.249
- In my head I'm like, okay.
They don't even see what I did,

01:05:29.249 --> 01:05:30.643
they don't know what they are doing.

01:05:31.596 --> 01:05:33.830
- Yeah, it's the worst beginning
in the world, isn't it?

01:05:33.830 --> 01:05:35.012
